{"step_index":35,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T01:18:01Z","content":"Priyanshu, the full research report is ready — check the artifact above.\n\nHere's what the research actually says, stripped of cheerleading:\n\n**The direct answer for your laptop purchase:**\n\n### Buy 16 GB dedicated VRAM (RTX 5080 class, ~₹1.5-2L range)\n\n**Why this number specifically:**\n- **8 GB is dead** — locks you into 7-8B models that can't do serious reasoning\n- **12 GB works today but will feel cramped by 2028** — the \"useful\" model size floor is moving from 14B toward 27B+\n- **16 GB is where you stop being frustrated** — handles today's 14B sweet-spot models (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B scores 93.9% on math benchmarks), will handle 27-35B models by 2028 as quantization and KV cache compression improve\n- **24 GB is better but costs ₹50K-80K more** — only worth it if you're doing image/video generation or want 32B+ models today\n\n**What the research challenged me on (counter-arguments I can't dismiss):**\n1. A \\$20/month ChatGPT Plus subscription gives you **better AI** than any local model on any laptop — local AI trades quality for privacy and offline capability\n2. Laptops thermal-throttle within 10-15 minutes of sustained inference, dropping speed 20-40% — desktop rigs are objectively better for this\n3. Reddit is full of people who bought high-VRAM laptops for AI and went back to cloud APIs within a year\n\n**The alternative path:** If you're open to Mac, an M5 Pro with 48 GB unified memory gives more raw capacity than any Windows laptop under \\$3,000 and runs 27-35B models today. Trade-off: slower per-token speed vs NVIDIA."}
